config BR2_PACKAGE_TEMURIN_JRE
	bool "temurin-jre"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_GLIBC
	help
	  Eclipse Temurin JRE, the Java runtime for the identity service
	  (geekdojo/geekdojo-brain#969). Installs Adoptium's pinned,
	  signature-verified release JRE to /usr/lib/temurin-jre, with an
	  empty PKCS-12 lib/security/jssecacerts and its licences under
	  /usr/share/licenses/temurin-jre/. The host variant, at the same
	  pin, is in $(HOST_DIR)/lib/temurin-jre.

	  Not enabled in any release until Identity 2.2.

	  The upstream binaries are linked against glibc. A build-time
	  check (check-needed.sh, a target-finalize hook) fails the build
	  when any ELF file in the installed JRE names a NEEDED library the
	  image does not carry.

	  There is deliberately no architecture "depends on": a target
	  architecture the tarball map in temurin-jre.mk does not know
	  fails the build instead of silently dropping the runtime.

	  https://adoptium.net

